2186562398 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186562337 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562398 #edb/ref 1069 "q-106275" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562398 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562398 #edb/ref 1071 "What is the domain of the function $f(x)=-3{x}^{2}+2x-8?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562398 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0df15b39-86c5-5700-94a4-0033b72fc48e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562398 #edb/ref 1074 "A quadratic function is defined for all real numbers.\n\nTherefore, the domain of $f(x)$ is $x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562401 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186562339 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562401 #edb/ref 1069 "q-90885" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562401 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562401 #edb/ref 1071 "What is the domain of the function $h(x)={x}^{2}-2x-3?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562401 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "148b6736-c231-507d-9d97-3fb2f60f3b61" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562401 #edb/ref 1074 "A quadratic function is defined for all real numbers.\n\nTherefore, the domain of $h(x)$ is $x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562403 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186562381 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562403 #edb/ref 1069 "q-154270" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562403 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562403 #edb/ref 1071 "What is the range of the function $f(x)=3{x}^{2}-6x+5?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562403 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "16afc9a4-390c-580b-b4f5-9f8ca64be1a7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562403 #edb/ref 1074 "The given parabola is written in standard form,\n\n$$\ny=a{x}^{2}+bx+c,\n$$\n\nwith $a=3>0,$ $b=-6,$ and $c=5.$\n\nBecause the leading coefficient is positive, the parabola opens upward. Consequently, there is no maximum output, and the vertex corresponds to the minimum output.\n\nThe $x$-coordinate of the vertex is given by\n\n$$\nx=-\\frac{b}{2a}=-\\frac{(-6)}{2\\cdot 3}=1.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute $x=1$ back into the function to find the $y$-value of the vertex:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =3{x}^{2}-6x+5 \\\\  & =3(1)^{2}-6(1)+5 \\\\  & =3-6+5 \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vertex is $(1,2),$ and the range of the function is $[2,\\infty ).$\n\n![](images/91/915c1435f78f8a5f85a104b40d9ee83c54c218f8e81b6ea7fc051367055fc624.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562408 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186562277 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562408 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186562371 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562408 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186562380 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562408 #edb/ref 1069 "q-250607" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562408 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562408 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the range of the function $f(x)=-3(x+5)^{2}+7.$\n\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}\n$f(x)\\le $\n{{field-3}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562408 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2002fa84-a05e-5e54-ad18-933be8248d10" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562408 #edb/ref 1074 "The parabola is written in vertex form, \n\n$$\ny=a(x-h)^{2}+k,\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ is the leading coefficient and $(h,k)$ is the vertex. \n\n- Since $h=-5$ and $k=7,$ the vertex is $(-5,7).$\n\n- Since $a=-3<0,$ the parabola opens downwards.\n\nBecause the parabola opens downwards, there is no minimum output, and the vertex corresponds to the maximum output.\n\nTherefore, the range is $(-\\infty ,7],$ i.e. $-\\infty <f(x)\\le 7.$\n\nThe corresponding diagram is shown below.\n\n![](images/25/252a3c0475f838b1835f2da9c3c818a938c916b781c5abaa1f12ed09c52c56f6.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562435 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186562230 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562435 #edb/ref 1069 "q-106272" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562435 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562435 #edb/ref 1071 "What is the domain of the function $f(x)=10(x+4)^{2}+5?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562435 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "52919907-6d33-5d25-ab23-9ceab696d862" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562435 #edb/ref 1074 "A quadratic function is defined for all real numbers.\n\nTherefore, the domain of $f(x)$ is $x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562437 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186562225 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562437 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186562249 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562437 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186562261 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562437 #edb/ref 1069 "q-250633" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562437 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562437 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the range of the function $f(x)=2{x}^{2}+8x+11.$\n\n{{field-1}}\n$\\le f(x)$\n{{field-2}}{{field-3}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562437 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "5e73f5fc-13ec-5727-bb90-2579fb0880d6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562437 #edb/ref 1074 "The given parabola is written in standard form,\n\n$$\ny=a{x}^{2}+bx+c,\n$$\n\nwith $a=2>0,$ $b=8,$ and $c=11.$\n\nBecause the leading coefficient is positive, the parabola opens upward. Consequently, there is no maximum output, and the vertex corresponds to the minimum output.\n\nThe $x$-coordinate of the vertex is given by\n\n$$\nx=-\\frac{b}{2a}=-\\frac{8}{2\\cdot 2}=-2.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute $x=-2$ back into the function to find the $y$-value of the vertex:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =2{x}^{2}+8x+11 \\\\  & =2(-2)^{2}+8(-2)+11 \\\\  & =8-16+11 \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vertex is $(-2,3),$ and the range of the function is $[3,\\infty ),$ i.e. $3\\le f(x)<\\infty .$\n\n![](images/3a/3a87830f59bf840ac8ab0d761ab7319b53fc804bc9d925e92850313d5d5a7a52.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562458 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186562301 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562458 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186562315 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562458 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186562346 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562458 #edb/ref 1069 "q-250639" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562458 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562458 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the range of the function $f(x)=-{x}^{2}+4x+1.$\n\n{{field-1}}\n$<f(x)$\n{{field-2}}{{field-3}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562458 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "89ea5a4a-e490-551f-988c-728a0c124eab" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562458 #edb/ref 1074 "The given parabola is written in standard form,\n\n$$\ny=a{x}^{2}+bx+c,\n$$\n\nwith $a=-1<0,$ $b=4,$ and $c=1.$\n\nBecause the leading coefficient is negative, the parabola opens downward. Consequently, there is no minimum output, and the vertex corresponds to the maximum output.\n\nThe $x$-coordinate of the vertex is given by\n\n$$\nx=-\\frac{b}{2a}=-\\frac{4}{2\\cdot (-1)}=2.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute $x=2$ back into the function to find the $y$-value of the vertex:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-{x}^{2}+4x+1 \\\\  & =-(2)^{2}+4(2)+1 \\\\  & =-4+8+1 \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vertex is $(2,5),$ and the range of the function is $(-\\infty ,5],$ i.e. $-\\infty <f(x)\\le 5.$\n\n![](images/ce/ce52355662b526af83614a6c4cbe6e7f2d7f07d379b2636d14e094d47e0e0da6.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562459 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186562268 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562459 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186562295 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562459 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186562353 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562459 #edb/ref 1069 "q-250644" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562459 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562459 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the range of the function $f(x)=(x-2)(x-8).$\n\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}\n$f(x)<$\n{{field-3}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562459 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8a31f28b-9e61-5b12-8422-c1bd2c17fb23" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562459 #edb/ref 1074 "The given parabola is written in factored form,\n\n$$\ny=a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2}),\n$$\n\nwith $a=1>0.$ \n\nBecause the leading coefficient is positive, the parabola opens upward. Consequently, there is no maximum output, and the vertex corresponds to the minimum output.\n\nThe two roots of the parabola are ${x}_{1}=2$ and ${x}_{2}=8,$ and we can find the $x$-coordinate of the vertex by taking the average of the roots:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2}=\\frac{2+8}{2}=5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $x=5$ back into the function to find the $y$-value of the vertex:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =(x-2)(x-8) \\\\  & =(5-2)(5-8) \\\\  & =3\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =-9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vertex is $(5,-9),$ and the range of the function is $[-9,\\infty ),$ i.e. $-9\\le f(x)<\\infty .$\n\n![](images/84/84c22aee72ebd52e3dab84a72ad1d402813c3a38794c653cd4cb0e31bfef3836.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562462 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186562254 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562462 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186562260 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562462 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186562369 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562462 #edb/ref 1069 "q-250649" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562462 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562462 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the range of the function $f(x)=-4(x-1)(x-4).$\n\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}\n$f(x)\\le $\n{{field-3}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562462 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8f69a422-81e0-551f-abc6-71d3ea93c826" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562462 #edb/ref 1074 "The given parabola is written in factored form,\n\n$$\ny=a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2}),\n$$\n\nwith $a=-4<0.$ \n\nBecause the leading coefficient is negative, the parabola opens downward. Consequently, there is no minimum output, and the vertex corresponds to the maximum output.\n\nThe two roots of the parabola are ${x}_{1}=1$ and ${x}_{2}=4,$ and we can find the $x$-coordinate of the vertex by taking the average of the roots:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2}=\\frac{1+4}{2}=\\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $x=\\frac{5}{2}$ back into the function to find the $y$-value of the vertex:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-4(x-1)(x-4) \\\\  & =-4(\\frac{5}{2}-1)(\\frac{5}{2}-4) \\\\  & =-4\\cdot \\frac{3}{2}\\cdot (-\\frac{3}{2}) \\\\  & =9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vertex is $(\\frac{5}{2},9),$ and the range of the function is $(-\\infty ,9],$ i.e. $-\\infty <f(x)\\le 9.$\n\n![](images/70/70dc863f5f089c9434d783495c31b77fd7a0ac84a852d2b32222b445f463efe3.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562470 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186562350 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562470 #edb/ref 1069 "q-106279" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562470 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562470 #edb/ref 1071 "What is the range of the function $f(x)=\\frac{1}{2}(x-8)^{2}-18?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562470 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a24bba0b-6082-5434-98a9-2578424db732" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562470 #edb/ref 1074 "The parabola is written in vertex form, \n\n$$\ny=a(x-h)^{2}+k,\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ is the leading coefficient and $(h,k)$ is the vertex. \n\n- Since $h=8$ and $k=-18,$ the vertex is $(8,-18).$\n\n- Since $a=\\frac{1}{2}>0,$ the parabola opens upwards.\n\nBecause the parabola opens upwards, there is no maximum output, and the vertex corresponds to the minimum output. \n\nTherefore, the range is $[-18,\\infty ).$\n\nThe corresponding diagram is shown below.\n\n![](images/a1/a115822cf26b79f0b25ed5493f5951c71c02c6ef5a4d576d101b4bc580d5da9f.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562475 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186562232 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562475 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186562248 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562475 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186562312 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562475 #edb/ref 1069 "q-250599" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562475 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562475 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the range of the function $f(x)=5(x+1)^{2}+8.$\n\n{{field-1}}\n$\\le f(x)$\n{{field-2}}{{field-3}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562475 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ae8713d7-4691-5e08-870e-3fc604e3a336" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562475 #edb/ref 1074 "The parabola is written in vertex form, \n\n$$\ny=a(x-h)^{2}+k,\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ is the leading coefficient and $(h,k)$ is the vertex.\n\n- Since $h=-1$ and $k=8,$ the vertex is $(-1,8).$\n\n- Since $a=5>0,$ the parabola opens upwards.\n\nBecause the parabola opens upwards, there is no maximum output, and the vertex corresponds to the minimum output.\n\nTherefore, the range is $[8,\\infty ),$ i.e. $8\\le f(x)<\\infty .$\n\nThe corresponding diagram is shown below.\n\n![](images/7f/7ff6f49b63c4ad55324bbb406558781c9f3e5af3a98d34b285c65f88746bddab.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562482 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186562245 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562482 #edb/ref 1069 "q-90888" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562482 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562482 #edb/ref 1071 "What is the domain of the function $g(x)=\\frac{1}{2}(x-1)^{2}-2?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562482 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b6f92520-185d-575d-8ae4-7a79216b322b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562482 #edb/ref 1074 "A quadratic function is defined for all real numbers.\n\nTherefore, the domain of $g(x)$ is $x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562498 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186562344 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562498 #edb/ref 1069 "q-90989" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562498 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562498 #edb/ref 1071 "What is the range of the function $f(x)=\\frac{1}{2}(x-2)(x+6)?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562498 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "da80a3c6-7cc5-5c7d-84d3-2b9e185bcdef" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562498 #edb/ref 1074 "The given parabola is written in factored form,\n\n$$\ny=a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2}),\n$$\n\nwith $a=\\frac{1}{2}>0.$ \n\nBecause the leading coefficient is positive, the parabola opens upward. Consequently, there is no maximum output, and the vertex corresponds to the minimum output.\n\nThe two roots of the parabola are ${x}_{1}=2$ and ${x}_{2}=-6,$ and we can find the $x$-coordinate of the vertex by taking the average of the roots:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2}=\\frac{2+(-6)}{2}=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $x=-2$ back into the function to find the $y$-value of the vertex:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{1}{2}(x-2)(x+6) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(-2-2)(-2+6) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (-4)\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =-8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vertex is $(-2,-8),$ and the range of the function is $[-8,\\infty ).$\n\n![](images/ba/bac4e1a79c32d61d6bc348564b2d791a06d19b0126c49af0689dd821d5063b4e.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562517 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186562216 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562517 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186562283 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562517 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186562304 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562517 #edb/ref 1069 "q-250645" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562517 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562517 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the range of the function $f(x)=\\frac{1}{5}(x+9)(x-1).$\n\n{{field-1}}\n$\\le f(x)$\n{{field-2}}{{field-3}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562517 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "fe465ece-00d7-560c-ae8f-64c0313299b0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562517 #edb/ref 1074 "The given parabola is written in factored form,\n\n$$\ny=a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2}),\n$$\n\nwith $a=\\frac{1}{5}>0.$ \n\nBecause the leading coefficient is positive, the parabola opens upward. Consequently, there is no maximum output, and the vertex corresponds to the minimum output.\n\nThe two roots of the parabola are ${x}_{1}=-9$ and ${x}_{2}=1,$ and we can find the $x$-coordinate of the vertex by taking the average of the roots:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2}=\\frac{-9+1}{2}=-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $x=-4$ back into the function to find the $y$-value of the vertex:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{1}{5}(x+9)(x-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}(-4+9)(-4-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot 5\\cdot (-5) \\\\  & =-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vertex is $(-4,-5),$ and the range of the function is $[-5,\\infty ),$ i.e. $-5\\le f(x)<\\infty .$\n\n![](images/97/97c587abebf09ff27a805db3b32b3c5f26b5d51baaf7f6827618e01ccdd53642.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
